WEBVTT

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:04.150
<i>The new continent of Patria.</i>

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.310
<i>One hundred years after immigrants</i>

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:10.760
<i>from the old continent established 
a new democratic nation here,</i>

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:15.100
<i>the discovery of a new energy ore 
called Somnium caused conflict</i>

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:19.630
<i>between the Northern City of Industry 
and the Southern City of Mining,</i>

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:22.400
<i>which erupted into civil war, 
splitting the nation.</i>

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.010
<i>The civil war that split the nation into</i>

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:39.200
<i>the Northern Union of Patria and the 
Southern Confederation of Patria</i>

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.730
<i>was dominated by the south, 
as they far outnumbered the north.</i>

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:45.880
Charge!

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:49.630
Fire!

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:11.210
Keep advancing!

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:23.670
The company commander is down!

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:06.980
Commence attack!

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:45.160
Fire!

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:46.550
Don't let them get inside!

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:48.110
Fire!

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:51.390
What's that?!

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:52.540
Something's there!

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:09.240
Stay back! Stay away from me, you monster!

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:12.760
Fire! Fire everything you've got!

00:03:58.390 --> 00:04:01.720
<i>Fearing defeat, the Northern government</i>

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:07.140
<i>used a forbidden technology to turn the tide</i>

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.700
<i>by creating unique soldiers.</i>

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:17.180
<i>Hideous-looking soldiers who overran 
the battlefield in the blink of an eye.</i>

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:27.480
<i>The people likened them to gods,
and called them "Incarnates."</i>

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:37.890
To think you captured a fortress that was 
considered impregnable this easily...

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:41.340
So the rumors about you were true,
Special Sergeant Major Henriette.

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:43.100
You honor me, Major.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:46.600
But due to our late arrival, 
many of our men lost their lives.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:48.610
Oh, don't you worry about that.

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:51.420
They gave their lives to help
secure the North's victory.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:53.430
What greater honor is there?

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:56.120
Anyway, good work out there.

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:57.870
Get some rest before the next mission.

00:04:57.870 --> 00:04:58.680
Yes, sir!

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:05.060
Incarnates are the product 
of top-secret research...

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:07.880
Can they really be trusted?

00:05:09.190 --> 00:05:11.860
They're nothing more than
weapons, Lieutenant.

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:14.070
We just have to use them properly.

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:19.650
We're coming in, Elaine.

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:20.760
Come in.

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:24.530
Thank goodness you're safe.

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:26.450
I'm glad to see you, Hank and Cain.

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:30.630
If that major was the one 
directing us out there,

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:33.180
we may have had the honor 
of dying on the battlefield.

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:35.880
Come on, now. You'll get in 
trouble if someone hears you.

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:38.390
So, how did the soldiers look?

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:43.150
There were only a few whose symptoms 
showed progression in this last battle.

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:44.270
I see.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:48.930
I'll figure something out. I'm the one 
who created the Incarnates, after all.

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:50.340
I swear I will.

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:55.400
Don't worry. All of our men believe in you.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:57.290
Of course, that goes for me, too.

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:05.420
Thank you, Hank.

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:12.380
So, uh...

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:15.530
Right, well, I'm gonna go check on the others!

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:17.980
For crying out loud...

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:20.870
Guess he's still the same snot-nosed kid.

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:37.750
So your daughter Schaal is running 
the orphanage on her own now?

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:40.490
I lost my wife when Schaal 
was still very young.

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:43.130
She does a wonderful job.

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:45.450
You seem very proud of her.

00:06:45.450 --> 00:06:46.250
I am.

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:52.060
Man... I wanna have a family 
with a girl like that someday.

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:54.930
I know! Introduce me to Schaal—

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:57.840
Will, you'd best pick anyone but Roy.

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:02.320
If someone doesn't live up to his ideals, 
he'll pin all the blame right on them.

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:04.810
I think you're talking about 
your wife who ran off, Eddie!

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:08.070
When the war's over, 
you should all come visit.

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:09.740
My daughter and the kids would be thrilled.

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:11.120
Hell yes!

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:12.060
Hey, are you sure about that?

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:13.660
Captain!

00:07:14.630 --> 00:07:16.010
At ease.

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:19.670
What's up, Roy?

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:21.490
You seem to be in a good mood.

00:07:21.490 --> 00:07:24.120
Take a look at Will's daughter, Captain.

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:26.580
He's gonna introduce me to her!

00:07:25.030 --> 00:07:26.730
Ooh, let me see!

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:29.550
He says she's a really good girl
who cares about her family!

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.370
Wow, she's cute.

00:07:28.370 --> 00:07:29.550
She really is!

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:30.980
Is that right?

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:33.080
Sorry. I might be a bit biased.

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:34.840
I just know it.

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:37.600
She's gonna grow up to be 
a beautiful young woman.

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:39.740
That's something to look forward to.

00:07:39.740 --> 00:07:43.490
What? I thought you only had 
eyes for Doctor Elaine, Captain.

00:07:43.490 --> 00:07:45.870
You shouldn't cheat on her, Captain.

00:07:45.870 --> 00:07:49.280
Yeah, Captain! Schaal is my—

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:51.620
What about Elaine?!

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:54.190
Wh-What do you mean?

00:07:54.190 --> 00:07:56.190
I was wondering about that, too.

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:57.400
She might run away if you wait too long.

00:07:56.190 --> 00:07:56.930
Me, too!

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:57.940
Better shape up.

00:07:56.930 --> 00:08:00.850
The doctor might be waiting for you 
to approach her, too, Captain.

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:02.460
I'll...

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:07.420
I'll think about it when the war's over...

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:13.980
What's going on? It looks like everyone's here.

00:08:13.980 --> 00:08:15.440
Cain! Ela—

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:18.550
Deputy Captain, listen to this! 
The captain and the doc—

00:08:19.170 --> 00:08:20.260
It's nothing!

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:21.740
What's this about me?

00:08:21.740 --> 00:08:22.720
Uh, it's nothing!

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:24.720
Take some initiative, Captain!

00:08:23.470 --> 00:08:24.970
What are you guys talking about?

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:25.790
Yeah!

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:26.000
Nothing!

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:28.000
Captain, Roy is foaming at the mouth.

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:27.370
You fail as captain.

00:08:35.330 --> 00:08:36.160
It's...

00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:38.160
The Incarnates!

00:09:53.870 --> 00:09:56.310
We settled this faster than expected.

00:09:56.310 --> 00:09:57.160
Yeah.

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:23.430
What is this?

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:30.350
Abi, what are you doing?!

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:30.830
Calm down, Abi!

00:10:29.880 --> 00:10:31.280
Abi, stop!

00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:34.620
Help!

00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:35.810
Prepare the cannons! Hurry!

00:10:35.810 --> 00:10:37.240
Abi, stop!

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:42.870
Hank, it's too dangerous!

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:44.320
Abi!

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:48.610
Why are you doing this?

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:50.830
Captain...

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:54.600
No... It's not me...

00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:57.210
Please... stop me.

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:01.510
Fire! Shoot him dead!

00:11:04.270 --> 00:11:05.230
Abi!

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:16.310
Abi! Are you all right?

00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:19.830
No... It's not me...

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:21.270
It's something el—

00:11:21.670 --> 00:11:22.840
Medic!

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:30.360
Someone! Get a medic over here!

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:33.770
I... I'm sorry...

00:11:34.990 --> 00:11:36.160
Abi, don't!

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:52.140
Am I going to end up like Abi someday?

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:52.890
No way...

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:55.000
No... I'm scared.

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:56.110
Shut up, Theo!

00:11:58.840 --> 00:12:02.140
A while back, he said...

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:05.770
Lately, when I fight as an Incarnate,

00:12:05.770 --> 00:12:09.440
I start wondering which one is the real me.

00:12:09.440 --> 00:12:09.950
What?

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:13.530
I wonder if, someday, I won't be 
able to turn back into a human...

00:12:13.890 --> 00:12:14.700
Abi?

00:12:14.700 --> 00:12:15.740
Just kidding!

00:12:16.050 --> 00:12:18.510
Sorry for being all weird.

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:23.020
Something must have already been 
happening to him back then.

00:12:23.670 --> 00:12:25.470
I even realized that...

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:28.420
But I couldn't do anything.

00:12:30.670 --> 00:12:34.050
Is there a possibility that this 
could happen to all of us?

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:38.770
I'm not sure... I really don't know. I'm sorry.

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:40.380
Elaine...

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:14.050
Listen up, everyone.

00:13:14.780 --> 00:13:17.900
We still don't know what 
made Abi go berserk.

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:21.330
There's still a lot we don't know 
about the power of Incarnates.

00:13:21.330 --> 00:13:25.350
There is a possibility that what happened 
to Abi could eventually happen to us.

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:28.540
But we are not beasts!

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:31.370
We are Incarnates, and we 
have our own will and pride!

00:13:31.990 --> 00:13:35.660
So right here, right now, 
we will swear an oath.

00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:38.840
Those who have lost their souls

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:40.830
shall be slain by their own.

00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:46.030
If something similar ever happens again,

00:13:46.030 --> 00:13:48.460
we should be the ones to stop it.

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:52.910
To make sure all the fighting we've done 
to end this war wasn't for nothing,

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:56.310
let's all face this together.

00:13:56.800 --> 00:13:59.060
We are never alone!

00:13:59.430 --> 00:14:01.430
Please don't forget that.

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:51.450
I thank you all for enduring 
 this highly demanding mission.

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:54.520
Tomorrow is finally the day 
we capture the capital.

00:14:54.820 --> 00:14:57.340
This will be our most intense fight yet.

00:14:57.340 --> 00:14:59.220
But if we make it through this...

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:08.300
Once this war is over, I'm...

00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:11.980
I'm going to ask Elaine to be with me.

00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:15.410
And I want all of you here 
to celebrate with me.

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:17.610
Captain's orders.

00:15:19.490 --> 00:15:21.190
Let's all come back alive.

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:27.710
Yeah!

00:15:25.570 --> 00:15:27.350
We can't be dying now!

00:15:27.350 --> 00:15:29.890
Let's hurry up and get this war over with!

00:15:32.330 --> 00:15:33.060
Hank...

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:36.340
Don't overwork yourself.

00:15:36.340 --> 00:15:38.480
Tomorrow's going to be an all-out battle.

00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:40.650
I want to do everything I possibly can.

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:45.930
All the battles we were assigned 
to were lost causes.

00:15:45.930 --> 00:15:50.670
We may be Incarnates,
 but surviving wasn't easy.

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:54.620
We only made it this far 
because you're our captain.

00:15:55.130 --> 00:15:56.980
I couldn't have asked for anyone better.

00:15:56.980 --> 00:15:58.780
No, that's not it.

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:03.210
It's because you all believed in me 
that I was able to get us this far.

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:05.410
It's everyone in the squad...

00:16:05.410 --> 00:16:09.170
as well as you and Elaine who made 
it possible for me to be the captain.

00:16:10.690 --> 00:16:12.030
Figures you'd say that.

00:16:12.430 --> 00:16:16.050
Do you remember when the 
three of us first met?

00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:16.990
Yeah.

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:20.660
Who would have thought that war orphans 
like us could become best friends

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:23.370
with a little rich boy from a 
distinguished family like you?

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:24.670
Indeed.

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:28.580
Hank, take good care of Elaine.

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:33.870
She's trying to deal with everything 
on her own, and it's crushing her.

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:37.510
You're the only one who can support her.

00:16:39.210 --> 00:16:41.000
Elaine, it's me.

00:16:46.090 --> 00:16:48.050
What did you want to talk about?

00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:51.930
Hank, this war will soon be over.

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:56.480
Tomorrow's operation will probably 
be called off right before it begins.

00:16:57.570 --> 00:17:01.040
HQ has been moving forward with 
top-secret ceasefire negotiations.

00:17:01.490 --> 00:17:04.510
The draft of the peace treaty
 is already complete.

00:17:04.510 --> 00:17:08.540
This country that was split into north 
and south is about to become one again.

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:09.960
Are you sure?

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:10.720
Yes.

00:17:17.450 --> 00:17:18.570
I see...

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:22.940
Peace will finally be upon us...

00:17:24.380 --> 00:17:26.980
But we'll have no place in that peace.

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:29.610
What do you mean?

00:17:40.730 --> 00:17:41.900
Elai—

00:17:45.700 --> 00:17:48.870
<i>What... My body... won't move...</i>

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:55.210
People who have become Incarnates will 
eventually lose not only their human forms,

00:17:55.210 --> 00:17:57.250
but their souls, as well.

00:17:57.580 --> 00:18:01.750
Every last one of them...
including you, Hank.

00:18:03.890 --> 00:18:06.550
When that happens, you'll lose all reason

00:18:07.070 --> 00:18:09.760
and become unable to control your powers.

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:13.460
I tried to find a way to avoid that,

00:18:14.450 --> 00:18:16.410
but I failed.

00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:20.750
If you all lose your human souls,

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:24.270
you'll be a greater threat 
than this war ever was.

00:18:25.050 --> 00:18:29.730
Before that happens, I need to do my duty

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:32.950
as the one who created the Incarnates.

00:18:33.610 --> 00:18:36.240
I can't let you all turn into beasts.

00:18:37.020 --> 00:18:40.800
Hank, you're too kind, 
so you'd probably try to stop me.

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:43.450
You'd make me hesitate...

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:45.360
So...

00:18:49.110 --> 00:18:52.340
Don't worry... I'll be following you soon.

00:19:00.460 --> 00:19:02.330
<i>Cain...</i>

00:19:07.690 --> 00:19:12.160
I'm sorry to have you help me with 
something I should be doing on my own.

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:17.080
As planned, we're going to 
kill everyone in the squad.

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:20.770
With these bullets, they should 
die without suffering.

00:19:21.330 --> 00:19:24.650
And then, when you and I die as well,

00:19:24.650 --> 00:19:27.760
everyone involved with the 
Incarnates will be gone.

00:19:28.240 --> 00:19:29.400
No...

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:23.730
You actually woke up!

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:27.320
Incarnates sure are resilient...

00:20:28.100 --> 00:20:29.290
Where am I?

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:30.780
The military hospital.

00:20:30.780 --> 00:20:33.890
I'm Second Lieutenant Liza Renecastle,
and I work for

00:20:33.890 --> 00:20:35.900
the Patria Union's military intelligence.

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:38.800
It's a pleasure to meet you, 
Special Sergeant Major Hank Henriette.

00:20:39.150 --> 00:20:42.190
You've been in a coma for two months.

00:20:42.190 --> 00:20:43.570
Two months?

00:20:43.570 --> 00:20:46.610
Yes. The war's long over, too.

00:20:50.010 --> 00:20:52.680
What happened to my squad?! To Elaine?!

00:20:53.570 --> 00:20:56.070
I'm actually here because 
I need to ask you about that.

00:20:58.070 --> 00:21:00.720
The day you were found on the verge of death,

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:04.950
Doctor Elaine Bluelake also disappeared 
and has been missing ever since.

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:07.660
The Incarnates squad was disbanded

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:11.710
and sent off to go wherever they 
wanted by Cain Madhouse.

00:21:11.710 --> 00:21:12.370
But...

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:15.500
Most of them started losing their sanity

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:18.130
and causing destruction 
wherever they went.

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:20.050
Many people have died.

00:21:20.990 --> 00:21:23.880
The Incarnates, once regarded as gods,

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:27.100
are now feared by the people...

00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:30.770
What in the world is going on? 
You must know something.

00:21:31.530 --> 00:21:34.110
Where is Cain?

00:21:34.470 --> 00:21:37.700
We lost contact with him shortly 
after the last battle.

00:21:44.440 --> 00:21:45.120
Cain!

00:22:09.750 --> 00:22:11.700
Help me!

00:22:13.800 --> 00:22:15.610
Edgar Beckford.

00:22:18.230 --> 00:22:24.360
I heard you've been going around killing 
your former comrades, Captain Hank.

00:22:27.960 --> 00:22:31.320
Those who have lost their souls 
shall be slain by their own.

00:22:31.690 --> 00:22:33.790
I came to fulfill our oath from that day!

00:22:34.130 --> 00:22:37.550
We became war heroes thanks to this power.

00:22:37.550 --> 00:22:39.330
No, we became gods!

00:22:39.330 --> 00:22:42.960
What's wrong with killing humans 
who defy the will of the gods?!

00:22:46.370 --> 00:22:50.510
Eddie! We have never been gods! 
Not in the past, and not now!

00:22:51.220 --> 00:22:53.350
And if we lose our souls,

00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:55.760
we're nothing more than beasts!

00:23:25.570 --> 00:23:27.380
Tea time, everyone!

00:23:27.380 --> 00:23:29.040
Will is this town's hero.

00:23:29.420 --> 00:23:30.800
I'm home, Mom.

00:23:31.220 --> 00:23:34.300
He killed my father...

00:23:34.300 --> 00:23:38.520
When the time comes for you to pull the 
trigger, I know you'll be able to do it.

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:39.970
The Dragon's Daughter
